        {
          "page": 4,
          "section": "2.4. Welding trials",
          "quote": "Welds in both Bead on plate (BOP) and butt joint configuration were produced on 3.2 mm thick sheets of Nb-1Zr-0.1C alloy using the aforementioned electron beam welding machine. Autogenous butt weld joints were made on 3.2 mm thick sheet specimens of Nb-1Zr-0.1C alloy with machined surfaces and during welding the specimens were held firmly using a fixture to prevent distortion. Different EB welds were produced by varying beam current from 30 to 60 mA and welding speed from 600 to 1200 mm/min (10 to 20 mm/sec). During these welding trials the specimens were kept inside an evacuated chamber (vacuum of the order of 10 -5 torr) at the beam focus position and the accelerating voltage was kept at 60 kV.",
          "table": null,
          "figure": null,
          "chunk_id": "9c74644723868aac:part:001"
        }
      ]
